Title:
COMegon — COM/RPC-based API dispatch and sleep framework (Zig)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
COMegon is a dual-mode Windows API dispatch framework that routes arbitrary function calls through COM runtime cross-apartment RPC so the observed call stack is system-only (combase.dll → rpcrt4.dll → ntdll.dll). It solves common OPSEC issues with thread-pool proxying and NtContinue/CONTEXT-based sleep obfuscation by using legitimate COM stub dispatch (NdrStubCall2) and fiber-based message pumping. In “Sleep mode,” it batches queued API calls as async RPC messages (PostCall) to enable sleep-time encryption chains (e.g., VirtualProtect + SystemFunction032 + NtDelayExecution) while no user frames remain on active stacks. In “Proxy mode,” it performs a synchronous single call (SendReceive) and returns an HRESULT, enabling “stack smuggling” for sensitive APIs. The project reconstructs COM/MIDL structures (MIDL_SERVER_INFO, stub descriptors, format strings, fake proxy/stub factory) and dynamically builds NDR proc format strings to describe parameters. It’s primarily useful for red teams, implant developers, and malware researchers focused on stealthy execution and sleep obfuscation; defenders can use it to understand COM/RPC-based execution paths that evade simplistic stack heuristics.

Technical Focus:
- COM cross-apartment marshaling and RPC dispatch (STA/MTA, IRpcChannelBuffer)
- MIDL/NDR internals (NdrStubCall2, Oi2 proc format strings, dispatch tables)
- Fiber-based execution and COM modal loop pumping (ModalLoop/CCliModalLoop)
- Sleep obfuscation via queued RPC messages (PostCall) and system-only call stacks
- Dynamic signature scanning of combase.dll internals for version resilience

Use Cases:
- Implementing sleep encryption chains without NtContinue/CONTEXT artifacts
- Executing sensitive WinAPI calls with “clean” COM/RPC-looking call stacks
- Building stealthy in-process loaders/agents that avoid common thread-pool proxy patterns
- Researching COM runtime internals and RPC-based execution tradecraft
- Developing/validating detections for anomalous COM proxy/stub registration and RPC message patterns

Keywords:
COM, DCOM, RPC, rpcrt4.dll, combase.dll, ntdll.dll, IRpcChannelBuffer, CoRegisterClassObject, CoMarshalInterThreadInterfaceInStream, CoGetInterfaceAndReleaseStream, STA, MTA, NdrStubCall2, MIDL_SERVER_INFO, MIDL_STUB_DESC, NDR format strings, PostCall, SendReceive, fibers, ModalLoop, CCliModalLoop, sleep encryption, SystemFunction032, NtDelayExecution, VirtualProtect, stack smuggling, Zig, CET shadow stack (/cetcompat)